498 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (Everyone keeps asking what you want to do with your life. Teachers, relatives, random adults at family gatherings who somehow think that's a perfectly normal thing to ask someone who still forgets to eat breakfast most mornings.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
499 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (And the worst part? You feel like you're supposed to have an answer. A real one. Something confident and specific that makes them nod approvingly and move on. So you say something vague and watch them look slightly disappointed, and you carry that feeling home like you've already failed at something.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
500 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (Here's what nobody tells you most people who have impressive, fulfilling careers today had absolutely no idea at that age. The person who confidently announced at 16 that they wanted to be a doctor either got lucky that it worked out, or spent years quietly changing direction without making a public announcement about it. Both are completely valid. Neither makes a better story than the other.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
