510 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E (Social media made comparison faster, easier, and completely inescapable. Someone is always doing better, looking better, achieving more at least from the outside.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
511 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E (But here's what the highlight reel never shows. The person whose grades you envy cried over that same subject two weeks ago. The one who looks effortlessly confident has a whole internal dialogue you'd never guess from their Instagram. Everyone is fighting something invisible. Everyone.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
512 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E (Comparison also has this sneaky way of making you compete in races you never actually signed up for. Suddenly you feel behind on a timeline that was never yours to begin with someone else's definition of success quietly became the standard you're measuring yourself against without even noticing.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
513 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E (The only comparison worth making is between who you were last month and who you are now. That's the only race where winning actually means something to your life.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
514 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E <FEFF00A000520075006C006500730020006F0066002000500072006F006300720061007300740069006E006100740069006F006E002C0020005700720069007400740065006E00200062007900200053006F006D0065006F006E00650020004700750069006C007400790020006F006600200041006C006C0020006F00660020005400680065006D>
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
515 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E (You know the feeling. The assignment has been sitting in your bag for four days. You're aware of it constantly while eating, sleeping, or watching videos it lives rent free in the back of your mind, making everything else slightly less enjoyable. And yet. You don't do it.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
516 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E (Procrastination can be seen as laziness from the outside view but it isn't. That's the first thing to understand. Lazy people don't feel guilty. Procrastinators feel guilty the entire time they're just paralyzed by some combination of anxiety, perfectionism, and the very specific pain of starting something hard from nothing.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
517 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E (The task feels enormous in your head. So you avoid it. And the longer you avoid it, the more enormous it becomes. That's the trap that avoidance makes anxiety grow, which makes avoidance more tempting, which makes the anxiety grow more. You're not procrastinating because you're bad at time management. You're procrastinating because the thing feels scary and starting feels worse than waiting.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
518 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
519 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E (Also, stop waiting to feel motivated. Motivation follows action it almost never precedes it. Nobody wakes up excited to write an essay. You sit down, you begin, and somewhere in the middle of it you find a rhythm. That rhythm was never going to arrive while you were lying down watching videos convincing yourself you'd start in twenty minutes.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
520 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E (Your future self is not a different, more disciplined, more energetic version of you. They're you, just later, with less time and the same amount of reluctance. Stop handing them your problems.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
