/E (These experiences teach them the importance of anticipation, organization, and consistent work in order to avoid last-minute issues. The club has notably participated in several major competitions, such as Course en Cours \(CeC\) and the World Robot Olympiad \(WRO\). )
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
634 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 161 0 R
/E (During these events, some members stood out for their commitment. For example, Abderrahmane Seiad and Achraf Essouli worked tirelessly to complete their project, even staying up several nights in a row to be ready for the national finals. Their experience perfectly illustrates the determination and sense of sacrifice required to succeed in this field. The club also emphasizes learning through failure. Defeats are not seen as obstacles, but as opportunities to improve. Members analyze their mistakes, identify their weaknesses, and continuously improve their projects. This approach allows them to strengthen their skills and build their self-confidence. Another key element of the club is teamwork. The success of a project does not depend solely on technical skills, but also on the ability of members to collaborate effectively. Task distribution, communication, and mutual support are essential to successfully complete projects. The club thus promotes an environment where everyone can learn from others and contribute according to their abilities. Finally, the robotics club stands out for its discipline and motivation. Members must demonstrate rigor, patience, and commitment in order to progress. Thanks to this mindset, the club not only trains skilled technicians, but also responsible, creative students who are ready to take on the challenges of the future.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
